@identity.sigil from Identity import { actor }
@rooms.sigil from Rooms import {
  room,
  room owner,
  room timezone,
  archived room,
}
@availability.sigil from Availability import {
  clock,
  open time,
  blackout,
  slot grid,
  repeated local time,
}
@booking.sigil from Booking import {
  booking request,
  requested range,
  request limits,
  renter,
  Pending,
  Confirmed,
  outside availability,
}

component Calendar {
  goal {
    Show an actor a *room calendar* of when a room is open and booked over a
    chosen *calendar range*, with detail that depends on who is looking.
  }

  logic {
    Building the room calendar reads open time and, for the room owner, each
    blackout from Availability, and reads each booking request overlapping the
    calendar range from Booking.

    It then projects each booking request for the actor, masking the renter on
    any booked block, and returns the room calendar.

    Each build of the room calendar also totals the Confirmed hours in the
    calendar range into a *booked hours total*.
  }

  constraints {
    A slot on the slot grid is requestable only when it lies within open time,
    overlaps no Confirmed booking request, starts after the clock and within the
    start horizon of the request limits, is
    not the second occurrence of a repeated local time, the actor is not the
    room owner, and the room is not an archived room;
    range-level rules are checked by Booking on submission.

    A slot whose end is the second occurrence of a repeated local time must not
    be selectable as an end slot, because Booking resolves that end to the
    earlier occurrence.

    The room calendar must pass the clock it receives to every Booking query and
    use only that clock wherever it compares a slot with now.

    A calendar range must span at most 31 days.

    A room calendar for an actor who is not the room owner must never reveal
    another renter or another renter's Pending booking request.

    On a fall-back date the room calendar shows each repeated local time twice.

    Booking request items that extend past the calendar range are clipped for
    display but keep their true start and end.

    The room calendar must not be cached; each read reflects the latest
    booking request state.
  }

  cases {
    Ana holds a Confirmed booking request; Ben's room calendar shows a booked
    block with no name and none of Ana's Pending items.

    A spring-forward date in America/New_York renders 23 hours of the slot grid
    on the room calendar.

    A calendar range of 32 days is refused.
  }

  interface {
    Calendar provides the room calendar of a room, shown in the room timezone
    with its zone label. Calendar assumes its caller passes the actor, the clock
    and a calendar range of room-local dates.

    For the room owner, the room calendar shows open time, each blackout, each
    Confirmed booking request with its renter and each Pending booking request,
    and marks each Confirmed one that is outside availability.

    Calendar requires the *renter display name* of each renter it shows to the
    room owner.

    For any other actor, the room calendar shows open time, other renters'
    Confirmed booking request items as an anonymous *booked block*, and that
    actor's own Pending and Confirmed booking request items marked as theirs.

    The room calendar marks each slot on the slot grid as requestable or not,
    so a renter selects a start slot and an end slot directly on it; the end
    slot is the last slot of the requested range, which runs from the start of
    the start slot to the end of the end slot, and a one-slot request selects
    the same slot twice.
  }

  decisions {
    Renter identity is masked as a booked block to protect renters, while the
    room owner keeps a full view to triage each Pending booking request.
  }
}
